eral delegation, and the pair is unmeasured; no in-authority, in-budget step moves the production decision; the record waits on Alex | in force | `reflection-6/codex-challenge-39.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:999:| D655 | 2026-11-17 | Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra (3 deciding targets, 2 reported, 5 controls, a share control; 52 sends, shared cap $3.60); verdict rules fixed before the send | in force | D655 record |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1021:| D677 | 2026-11-19 | The release comparison's goal loop closed: the old system stays, no paid work continues; reversed only if Alex reverses D505 or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first (council consensus, D439/D544) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-c-codex.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1028:| D684 | 2026-11-20 | Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the phase-1 iteration to Claude under the council loop (D439 limits); fresh pool of 116 answers as of 09-06 that the design never read | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1033:| D689 | 2026-11-20 | Alex chooses option 1: poc-v118 stays production, the hybrid's release line is paused, the release bar unchanged; council N (fresh Codex thread, consensus) closes the judge line and the c8 reading line for now under D543, D198 unchanged, nothing sent; reopening: judge on eight eligible failures on fresh questions plus matched controls and a source-checked summary (D198 option 2), then Alex's choice and funding; c8 on a traced decisive fact it delivers that old missed; D439 accounting error recorded ($39.65–$44.42 under two readings; $0 available without Alex) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1057:| D713 | 2026-11-21 | Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes): judging-v12 = judging-v7 with closed per-request id lists from the rendered rows (shared evidence enum, maxItems 0 when empty), one owner of membership, validator maxItems, preflight on saved judge formats, poc-v121; build and the $0 test T1–T5 next | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1058:| D714 | 2026-11-21 | judging-v12 and poc-v121 built (suite 388, mutants 12/12); every registered $0 check passes: old-2 replayed under v12 equals old-2 (1,616 judge answers through the closed format), all 5,391 valid stored answers fit and all 17 refused ones are excluded; provider acceptance and source choice need a paid step Alex opens | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1059:| D715 | 2026-11-22 | Alex approves $0.50 for judging-v12's paid acceptance step (\"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"): provider acceptance, then the 17 stored refused requests and 17 matched accepted ones, three sends each, read by hand against their sources; the reading rule agreed with the council before the send | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4874:- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4875:- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4876:- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4879:## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4881:- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4889:- **Next:** the council chooses the next step toward the PRD's production goal (D439).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4891:## D442 · 2026-11-13 · Next step: D431's same-day end-to-end comparison, run as a diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4897:## D443 · 2026-11-13 · Shape B': an exploratory census of final-answer losses, the stored clean chain against fresh production v118 draws (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4902:## D444 · 2026-11-13 · Three fresh production draws under a corrected ledger, replacing the stopped ones (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4908:## D445 · 2026-11-13 · Next: a $0 source-to-answer trace of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses, memory first (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4913:## D446 · 2026-11-13 · A $0 audit of a narrow typed-unit contract on the stored losses and correct controls (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4918:## D447 · 2026-11-13 · The typed-unit line stops; next a reviewed $0 design for wiring the ladder step end to end and its diagnostic same-day run (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4923:## D448 · 2026-11-13 · The wiring contract is settled; build and prove at $0, then review the code (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4928:## D449 · 2026-11-13 · The wiring's code review: four structural rules, two changes to the run states (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4967:## D450 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the slice: one fresh day through the wired path, live, on its own $1.50 ledger (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4984:## D451 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the full run: three clean draws and three production draws, same day, ledger $14.84 (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4999:## D452 · 2026-11-13 · The reading plan for the full run (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5013:## D453 · 2026-11-13 · Redo c2's Step 1 (a dropped response; council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5022:## D454 · 2026-11-13 ·