\": \"none\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n  },\n  \"collision\": {\n    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"collision-v2\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n  }\n}\n- **Since (D460–D462):** the whole-request audit of clean Step 1 (two readers apart, `step1-audit/AUDIT.md`) finds the standard's identity\n  boundaries missing from its request (the unsigned deal beside a plan's amount; another year of a shared quantity) and one date sentence\n  narrower than the standard (F6); F6 decided only one or two of 26 memory declines (`step1-audit/f6/`) and is recorded, not tested alone.\n  The status report for Alex, reviewed by the council for accuracy: `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/STATUS-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md`.\n- **Since (D463–D464):** the identity lever is a prompt clause first; candidate c16 (version 5, four blind audits) and a case-specific\n  diagnostic on fresh articles (one story per target boundary is all this window holds), 7 merge and 9 negative stories and the stored guards\n  (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/v2/PROBE-DESIGN-v2.md`).\n- **Since (D465–D466):** the identity diagnostic moved its error (c16 not adopted, c8 stays; `identity-probe/v2/RESULT.md`, $4.49); a deep\n  reflection council (Alex's request) agreed the second half of the day circled and reset the plan.\n- **Since (D467–D473):** the ladder-cost proofs are kept as tools (`ladder-cost/`); the ladder-refusal candidate stopped on a contested\n  \"main figure\" boundary; the 41 Stage A reader splits recorded, none changing its verdict; the ten right-by-refusal theses traced; the period\n  candidate c17 failed its frozen lines (memory and federal openings suppressed; `period-probe/RESULT.md`). Step 1 sentence changes on these\n  articles stop (D473). Provisional choices under D439 (D469): empty-start measurement; the three open shapes stay concerns; the written-ladder\n  line stands (D471). Alex's answer overrides any of them.\n- **Since (D474–D477):** the unsigned-deal candidate c18 was not adopted (`unsigned-deals/RESULT.md`). The source check of the eleven\n  first-pass refusals (`reachability/RESULT.md`): six right, four reachable only on paper, one split. **D477:** Stage A not passed; no theme or\n  ladder change for the H100 boundary; no more Step 1 sentence changes on these articles; production stays the default; the clean path's\n  three product choices are written for Alex (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CHOICES-FOR-ALEX-2026-11-13.md`).\n- **Since (D478–D482), under D439:** choice 2 tested and failed (c19); choice 3 taken (production stays the default); production's price\n  rule (D191.4) tested and failed (`docs/research/2026-11-13-shared-quantity-price/`); no further paid test on the frozen ruler (D482).\n- **Alex active again (2026-11-14).** D483–D486: a use-oriented acceptance was designed and its $0 trial read\n  (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/TRIAL-RESULT.md`); Alex asked for a leaner path (small steps, each run fast). D487: step 1 built nothing (the\n  \"dated after the article\" statements are correct dates against items stored a day early); step 2 runs one fresh week (2026-09-22..28, 235\n  items proved identical for both systems), one draw a system, a one-day slice first, readings A and B, the decision rule written before\n  reading (`LEAN-LOG.md` §2). Slice passed; production's week draw complete; the clean draw stopped twice on dropped connections, root-caused and fixed (D488: Step 1 resends a\n  network loss, each attempt on the ledger). The clean week draw completed from empty (`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/`, $2.52; both ledgers $4.69). **Result (D489,\n  `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md`):** not clear by the rule written before reading; no system chosen. Production\n  covers 4 of the 5 big matters two blind reader families listed, the clean path 2 (it lacks revenue and margin by D382/D384); judgement\n  support does not rank them at this size. The question then put to Alex (whether the new system holds questions on the company's main\n  numbers) was answered by him on 2026-11-15 (D505; see \"One next task\").\n  Recorded spend under D439 at that point: about $18.4 of $40 (about $7.26 before the run; the run's ledger $11.43, somewhat above its cost at the\n  published rates); the current figure is in \"One next task\". (An earlier line here gave \"about $29.2\" as tracked spend; no decision or\n  log records that figure and it is withdrawn.)\n- **Open defects recorded by this review:** the frozen judge retried 10, 16 and 18 judgements in the seeded clean draws, 38 of 51\n  reasons a theme cited as a dependency (PRD 11, E4), and its stored path holds the 2026-07-05 fault above (frozen; findings for\n  Alex); the same matter takes different shapes between draws (Kyber due end-2027 in one draw and end-2028 in another); under D397\n  the second bet of a topic that holds two has no answer; five-state event ladders failed by hand three times before a construction now in the request\n  produced ones that pass a reader; in Stage A the model's own are faulted by both reader families in 10 of 17 for the company.\n- **The unseeded measurement (D395):** graded subset 4.0 against 6.33 seeded. Every miss is a question not opened in the ruler's shape.\n  Judged answers 16 of 16, on the ruler's wording and ladder; the system's own questions have never met a judge.\n- **Stage 2 of D392:** clean 18, 18, 17 against v108 17, 15, 16, inconclusive on q12.\n- **Known gap (D394):** capital spending (q12).\n\nNo long job is running.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,160p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md; sed -n '161,280p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md; cat docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,160p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md; sed -n '161,280p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md; cat docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Citation-only judge version: closed id lists in the answer format (design v3, D712)\n\n**Alex's decision (D712, 2026-11-21):** \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\". The question offered: every id field of the judge's answer takes\na closed list built from the request; a $0 check on stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; any\npaid test asks him again.\n\n**Scope:** the answer format's four id fields, and the checks needed to enforce them:\n- the local validator's `maxItems`;\n- preflight reading each call's saved format.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- the prompt text;\n- the request text;\n- the rung field;\n- `check_answer` and its retry;\n- any retry policy;\n- what evidence is shown;\n- the link direction (a separate design, D711).\n\nv2 answers council round 38 (`codex-r38.md`): the format-error path, the batch and resume cells, duplicate theme pushes, preflight,\nthe D358 sizes, lists from the rendered rows, an unused version name, and the T1 proof.\n\nv3 answers round 38b (`codex-r38b.md`):\n- one owner of membership: under v12, `check_answer` uses the same row-built lists;\n- preflight reads the saved format of judge rows only;\n- the v7/v8 path keeps calling `build_prompt`;\n- a format error on the retry;\n- `maxItems: 0` keeps the item types;\n- T1's exact assertions;\n- T2 described as evidence from archived text, with a footnote control.\n\n## 1. Census (stored data, $0)\n\n- **Refusals.** Every refused judge answer on the stored runs is an id-membership error: an id outside the list its field allows.\n  - Population (Codex r37b and r38, reproduced by Claude's `id_typo_census.py`): 5,415 archive rows, 5,408 distinct request-answer\n    pairs, 5,389 committed, 17 refused, 2 valid answers of the stopped control batch never committed. Sources: old-1, old-2, old-3,\n    and the pilots' fresh rows.\n  - The classes:\n    - a one-character copy of a listed evidence id (e3620 → e362);\n    - a garbled evidence id (`e393`);\n    - a theme id in `cites_views` or in an evidence field;\n    - a dependency id used as an evidence id.\n- **The same class halted a run before (D358, 2026-10-28).** The sealed three-month run's Data Center request showed 698 evidence\n  ids; \"the model mislabels one id among dozens of pushes about every other attempt, the code refuses the answer, two refusals halt\n  the day\".\n- **List sizes per request**, counting evidence twice (cites and push ids) plus themes, dependencies and the two 3-value push enums:\n  - the five archives: max 915 (old-1 call 5652: 451 evidence ids);\n  - the sealed D358 archive: 10 of 949 requests over 1,000; call 6918 has 647 evidence ids, which is 1,323 values as plain enums and\n    676 if one shared evidence enum counts once.\n- **Provider limits** (OpenAI structured outputs guide, read 2026-11-21):\n  - \"up to 1000 enum values across all enum properties\";\n  - above 250 values, at most 15,000 characters per string enum;\n  - 120,000 characters in all;\n  - `minItems`/`maxItems` and `$defs`/`$ref` are supported;\n  - the guide is silent on empty enums and on how a referenced enum counts.\n\n## 2. Mechanism\n\nEvery request's closing line already forbids the wrong ids (`judging.py` lines 180–182). The answer format accepts any string there\n(`schema_for`, lines 55–75), so the model breaks the prose rule: about 0.3% of answers, 2.6% of linked readers', and every other\nattempt on a 698-id request (D358).\n\nThe code already decides membership after the answer (`check_answer`). Moving the same set into the format makes a wrong id\nunwritable: code owns identity (AGENTS §2). The judge still decides which evidence matters and how it pushes.\n\n## 3. The change\n\n- **One new version, `judging-v12`** (unused name; `judging-v9` named an earlier experiment):\n  - It has judging-v7's text and request, with closed lists. Its prompt file is a byte copy pinned to v7's sha.\n  - `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` gains it. `schema_for('judging-v7')` and `schema_for('judging-v8')` keep `JUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA`.\n  - Config: `poc-v121` = poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v12.\n  - No v8-based version is built. The shared list builder is proven on linked-1's saved v8 requests offline (T2).\n- **The lists come from the rows that render the request**, not from parsing its text:\n  - one function returns the system text, the user text and the three id lists from the same objects at the same store state:\n    - evidence: the `pieces` it prints;\n    - dependencies: the resolved dependencies that get an entry (a waiting dependency has no citable target);\n    - themes: the themes it prints;\n  - `build_prompt` keeps its signature and returns the first two;\n  - for v7 and v8, `round_of_judgements` still calls `build_prompt`, so the harness hooks that wrap it keep working;\n  - for v12 it calls the new function, which `build_prompt` also delegates to, so the text is rendered in one place;\n  - each v12 view's schema is built from its lists, and `ask` sends it, the retry included;\n  - the lists are not fooled by an id inside a multiline quote or reasons (Codex r38 counterexamples).\n- **One owner of membership under v12.** `check_answer` takes the same lists for v12 and checks evidence, theme and dependency\n  membership against them, not against the parsed text.\n  - Why: the text parser can narrow as well as widen. A quote holding a blank line followed by \"[\" ends the evidence block early, so\n    a real later id would be refused (Codex r38b).\n  - v7 and v8 keep the text parser unchanged (frozen). That latent narrowing is recorded as a finding, not fixed there.\n  - Under v12, a citation the format accepts can still take `check_answer`'s retry for a non-membership reason.\n- **The format.**\n  - One `$defs` string enum of the evidence ids, sorted, referenced by `cites.items` and `pushes.items.evidence_id`.\n  - A plain enum of the dependency ids for `cites_views.items`.\n  - A plain enum of the theme ids for `theme_pushes.items.view_id`.\n  - An empty list gives its array `maxItems: 0` and keeps its item type: a string for `cites` and `cites_views`; the full object for\n    `pushes` and `theme_pushes`, with its id field an open string. No empty enum is written.\n  - The schema name stays `judgement`.\n- **The local validator** (`model.check_schema`) gains `maxItems`, the mirror of `minItems`. No existing schema uses it (grep), so\n  no current answer changes status.\n- **Preflight part A**, judge rows only, checks each stored refused row against the format saved in that row's request\n  (`request_json.response_format.json_schema.schema`).\n  - A judge row without a saved format is reported as such, not skipped.\n  - Extraction and matching rows keep their current paths. A Jev row's request has no `response_format` (Codex r38b).\n- **Size.**\n  - No pre-send counting rule: the provider's counting of a referenced enum is unverified, and a guessed rule could refuse a\n    request the provider accepts.\n  - A request the provider refuses comes back as HTTP 400, which the transport raises at once without retrying (`openai_transport`).\n    It goes through `judge_day`'s generic path to `judging_failed`, and the day is resumable. A resume sends the same oversized\n    request and hits the same limit; that visible stop is the behaviour until a design change.\n  - No rule drops evidence to fit.\n\n## 4. Tables\n\n### 4.1 State × event\n\n| State / event | What happens | What is written; which date |\n|---|---|---|\n| First judgement | the lists are built as for any request | as now |\n| No dependency (all of poc-v121) | `cites_views` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n| No theme | `theme_pushes` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n| No evidence printed | `cites` and `pushes` have `maxItems: 0` (eligible views have evidence in force, but the printed set can be empty) | — |\n| A membership error from the provider (should not occur under strict mode) | `model.check_schema` refuses it: the row is saved with `:schema:`, `SchemaError` is raised, and the error reaches `judge_day`'s generic `judging_failed` path (not `judgement_refused_twice`, and no retry) | the refused row, suffixed; the day is resumable; a resume re-samples |\n| A `check_answer` refusal not about membership (rung range, a rung move without changed, an empty stance, a duplicate theme push) | the retry carries the same schema; a second refusal → `judgement_refused_twice` | as now |\n| A format error on the retry | `SchemaError` → `judging_failed`; judgements of earlier views in the same level may already be committed | those judgements stay; a resume skips them |\n| Several workers in a level, one fails | other workers' answers may already be saved, while the level records no judgement; on resume, committed judgements are skipped and saved answers are reused when the rebuilt request is byte-equal | as now |\n| Resume after a config or input change | a different request means a new key and a fresh answer; the default parallel runner may refuse the changed config or input before judging resumes (`parallel_day._manifest`) | as now |\n| A theme closes, or a dependency resolves, after the request is built | the lists are frozen in the sent format, and under v12 `check_answer` uses the same lists | — |\n| The provider refuses the format (HTTP 400: size or keyword) | not retried by the transport → `judging_failed` → resumable; a resume hits the same limit | no answer row |\n| A valid id that names the wrong source | not detectable by code | measured separately (§6) |\n\n### 4.2 Value × reader\n\n| Value | Reader | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| The per-request schema | `model.build_request`, then `request_identity` (archive key) | every v12 judge request has a new key: no stored answer is reused; any paired run needs its own replay proof |\n| The schema name `judgement` | `paid_run.is_judgement_request`, `july_test` | unchanged |\n| The saved format | preflight part A | read per judge row (changed, above) |\n| `build_prompt` | the paid_run and july_test prompt hooks | still called for v7/v8; a v12 harness hooks the new function |\n| The answer | `vocabulary.judgement_answer`, `_record` | the same shape |\n| The input size | cost | about 450 characters at the median, up to about 3,700 at the five archives' max with the shared enum; priced at $0.10 per million input tokens; measured in the $0 test |\n\n### 4.3 New path × old checks\n\n| Old check | Under v12 |\n|---|---|\n| `check_answer` membership | under v12, checked against the same lists as the format, so it cannot fire on an answer that passed; v7/v8 unchanged |\n| Rung range, first-judgement changed, rung move needs changed, stance non-empty, duplicate theme push | unchanged |\n| Frozen tests | v7/v8 unchanged; v12's prompt sha = v7's; a pinned schema on a fixed list |\n| D359 (only named versions are built) | `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` gains `judging-v12` only |\n| Launchers | poc-v121 is a product config like poc-v118 |\n\n### 4.4 Prior decisions\n\n- D354 and D712: the frozen judge, now opened by Alex.\n- D359: the code builds only named versions.\n- D694: a new name for a request change.\n- D198: the closed set is what the request showed.\n- D358: the evidence-bloat halts, the same class.\n- D711: the census and the recommendation.\n- The pre-v74i extraction admission schema constrained `folds_into` to the shown ids. It was removed with the frozen prompt (commit\n  248ef1b4); no decision rejected it.\n\n## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n\n### T1: the product path\nold-2 is replayed under poc-v121 through `replay.run`, serial path.\n- **The archive.** A scratch archive seeded with old-2's non-judge calls only, so every judge request misses it and reaches the\n  transport and the real validator.\n- **The transport.**\n  - It finds each judge request's stored old-2 call by its (system, user) bytes; the 1,620 pairs are unique (Codex r38).\n  - It asserts that the outgoing request equals the stored one in every key except the format.\n  - It asserts that the format has `strict: true` and the name `judgement`, and differs from v7's only in the four citation\n    constraints and the `$defs` they use.\n  - It asserts that each of the outgoing lists (evidence, dependencies, themes) equals the ids the request shows, read from its text\n    (evidence and theme entries; dependency entries).\n    - A mismatch is listed with its call and read by hand: a parser case is told from a builder bug before T1 can pass.\n    - An extra or missing id in any list fails T1. Codex r38c added an unlisted theme to 1,471 formats and every stored answer still\n      validated, so validation alone cannot catch it.\n  - It returns the stored answer, which goes through the real `model.call` and `model.check_schema`.\n  - Any other request (a non-judge miss, an unknown pair) stops the replay.\n- **The four refused first calls** (e88, e3955, e3998, theme ids). Each gets the saved accepted retry answer, labelled as a\n  substitution: under strict mode the provider could not have returned the refused one. All four retry answers fit their first\n  requests (Codex r38b). The four retry-note requests are not reached and are tested apart (T1b).\n- **Pass.**\n  - Exactly 1,616 judge responses through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions.\n  - The replay completes.\n  - The store equals old-2's on every table, listed explicitly from `sqlite_master`, with the expected differences named:\n    timestamps, archive call ids, request hashes, config checksum and version, and new empty tables.\n    - Judgements are compared on every substantive field: view, sequence, input, rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites,\n      `cites_views`, pushes, theme pushes, changed, `why_changed`, publication day.\n    - Every other table is compared on all its columns but the named ones (handovers, match records, days completed and the rest).\n  - New request hashes and the config are checked apart.\n\nT1 does not touch provider acceptance (§6).\n\n### T1b: the four originals\nEach refused original goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id `check_answer`\nrefused.\n\n### T1c: a real v12 retry\n- A store fixture with a theme in force; a fake provider answers the first v12 request with a duplicate theme push, which\n  `check_answer` refuses, then answers the retry correctly.\n- Assert that the retry request carries exactly the first request's format, citation lists included, and the retry note.\n- Mutant: the retry sent with the open v7 format must fail this test.\n\n### T5: preflight on a judge row without a saved format\nA refused judge row whose request has no `response_format` makes `scripts/preflight.py` exit non-zero, with the row named.\nToday `main` ignores part A's result, so it also needs a failing exit for this case. Extraction and matching rows keep their\npaths.\n\n### T2: every stored shape, offline (evidence from archived text)\n- For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are taken from the saved text. These are\n  archived calls whose store state is gone.\n- The parser can widen or narrow a list (the footnote case), so T2 is evidence from the archived text. T1 covers the built path.\n- Each answer is validated through the real `check_schema` with the v12 format.\n- Pass:\n  - all 5,389 committed answers and the 2 uncommitted valid ones validate;\n  - all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id;\n  - the population is printed as in §1.\n\n### T3: the real validator's controls\nFor all four fields, through `model.check_schema`:\n- an allowed id passes;\n- an unlisted id fails.\n\nAn empty list with `maxItems: 0` passes `[]`, and fails one otherwise valid item of the right type with an array-length error,\nnot a type error.\n\nT3 fails on today's validator, which ignores `maxItems`.\n\n### T3b: one owner of membership\n- A rendered request whose evidence quote holds a blank line followed by \"[1]\", with a real evidence entry after it. The v12 lists\n  include the later id, and `check_answer` under v12 accepts a citation of it.\n- The same answer under v7's text parser is refused. This control shows the parser case is real.\n\n### T4: sizes\nThe largest format over the five archives and over the sealed D358 archive is printed: evidence count, enum values with the\nreference counted once and counted twice, and characters.\n\n### Mutants\nEach is caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n- push ids left open;\n- lists parsed from the text instead of taken from the rows (the multiline-quote case);\n- `check_answer` under v12 reading the text instead of the lists (T3b);\n- `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n- `maxItems` removed from the validator;\n- `strict` dropped from the outgoing format (T1);\n- preflight reading the fixed schema for judge rows.\n\n### Also\n- Prompt size: the format's characters and tokens before and after, median and max.\n- The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.\n\n## 6. What the $0 test cannot show\n\n- **Provider acceptance of the exact format:** the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and a largest request (D358 call 6918's size).\n- **Whether the judge picks the intended source when constrained:** e3111 could become e3110 or e3112.\n- **Whether the forecasts move.**\n\nA paid step, Alex's to open, settles these. It would first send the largest stored request and an empty-list request to check\nacceptance, then re-send the stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones, and read the cited sources beside the\nforecasts.\n# Citation-only judge version: build and $0 test result (D714)\n\n**Verdict:** judging-v12 and poc-v121 are built, and every registered $0 check passes (DESIGN.md §5, registered before the runs;\nD713). No paid call was made. Provider acceptance of the format, and whether the judge then picks the intended source, remain for\na paid step that is Alex's to open (D712).\n\n## What was built (uncommitted)\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `src/hivemind/views/judging.py` | `judging-v12` added to `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS`, plus `CLOSED_LISTS` |\n| | `schema_for(version, lists)` closes the four id fields for v12: one shared `$defs` evidence enum, plain dependency and theme enums, `maxItems: 0` when a list is empty |\n| | `request_parts` returns the texts and the lists from the same rows; `build_prompt` delegates to it |\n| | `check_answer(..., lists)` checks membership against the lists under v12 |\n| | `round_of_judgements` sends each v12 view its own format, the retry included; v7/v8 still go through `build_prompt` with the frozen format |\n| `src/hivemind/model.py` | `check_schema` enforces `maxItems` |\n| `src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v12.txt` | a byte copy of judging-v7 (sha `d499c4b8…`) |\n| `poc/config/poc-v121.json` | poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v12 |\n| `scripts/preflight.py` | part A checks judge rows against their saved format; a judge row without one, a malformed one included (Codex r39), fails `main` with exit 1 |\n| `tests/test_citation_lists.py` | 7 tests: T1c, T3, T3b, T5 (part A, and `main`'s exit) and the format-error path |\n| `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` | 1 new test: the v12 prompt and two v12 formats pinned; the v7/v8 format sha unchanged |\n| `tests/test_live_lock.py` | part A's stub returns the new pair |\n\n**Checks of the build**\n- Suite: 388 passed, rerun after the preflight fix. The frozen tests are part of it.\n- `docs/check.py`: OK, rerun after the documents were updated.\n- Mutants: 12 of 12 caught, each by its own assertion (`mutants.log`). The failing assertion of each of the first 11 was read; the\n  12th is the malformed-row ordering.\n\n## The registered $0 checks\n\n| Check | Result | Record |\n|---|---|---|\n| **T1** old-2 replayed under poc-v121 | **PASS** | `poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/t1-result.json`, `t1-replay.log` |\n| **T1b** the four refused originals | **PASS** | same file |\n| **T1c** a real v12 retry | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n| **T2** every stored shape, offline | **PASS** | `t2-result.json`, `t2-offline.log` |\n| **T3** the real validator's controls | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py` |\n| **T3b** one owner of membership | **PASS** | same |\n| **T4** sizes | printed | `t2-result.json` |\n| **T5** preflight on a judge row without a format | **PASS** | `tests/test_citation_lists.py`; on old-2's real archive, part A checks its 4 refused judge rows against their saved format and preflight ends `preflight done` (`preflight-old2.log`) |\n\n### T1, old-2 replayed under poc-v121\n- 1,616 judge responses went through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions: 591→596, 6955→6979, 7068→7073, 7774→7780.\n- Every request equals old-2's outside the format.\n- Every format is strict, named `judgement`, and differs from judging-v7's only in the four constraints.\n- 0 list mismatches against the ids the text shows.\n- The store equals old-2's on all 36 shared tables, apart from the named columns:\n  - timestamps: `days_completed.at`, `processing_steps.at`, `views.created_at`;\n  - the judgements' `call_id`, `request_sha256` and `config_checksum`.\n- Positive control: one judgement's `why_changed` changed in a copy is reported as different.\n\n### T1b, the four refused originals\nEach goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id the check had refused: `e88`,\n`e3955`, `v10`, `e3998`.\n\n### T1c, a real v12 retry\nThe retry carries the first request's exact format and lists, plus the note.\n\n### T2, every stored shape\n- Population: 5,415 rows; 5,408 distinct pairs; 5,389 committed; 17 refused; 2 valid uncommitted.\n- Every committed and every valid uncommitted answer validates.\n- Every refused answer fails on its bad id:\n  - e362, e3111, e393;\n  - e88, e3955, e3998, e1382, e2769, e693;\n  - theme ids in cites (`v6`, `v10`);\n  - the dependency `v14` as evidence, twice;\n  - `v5` in `cites_views`, four times.\n\n### T3, the real validator's controls\nIn all four fields, an allowed id passes and an unlisted id fails. An empty list allows only `[]`, and a correctly typed item fails\non length.\n\n### T3b, one owner of membership\n- With a footnote in a quote, the v12 lists and the check accept the later real id.\n- v7's text parser refuses it. That narrowing is a latent defect of the frozen versions, recorded and not fixed there.\n\n### T4, sizes\n- Over the five archives the largest request has 451 evidence ids: 464 enum values with the shared enum counted once, 915 counted per\n  reference; 5,225 characters.\n- In the sealed D358 run the largest has 647 ids: 676 counted once, 1,323 per reference. 10 of 949 requests exceed the documented\n  1,000 if the provider counts per reference; none if it counts once.\n\n### Format size\n- Characters: judging-v7's format is 1,031; v12's median is 1,396–1,405 and its max 5,225.\n- Tokens, an estimate with o200k_base on the format's JSON over all 5,415 stored requests (the provider's own count arrives with the\n  paid step): v7 315; v12 median 502, p99 1,542, max 2,621.\n- At $0.10 per million input tokens, the largest request costs about $0.00023 more.\n\n## Deviations, disclosed\n\n- **T1's first run** (`poc/data/citation-t1-2026-11-21/`) completed the replay, but the comparison crashed: a harness defect, since\n  FTS tables have no rowid. The transport's log was lost with it.\n  - The fixed comparison on that store found three differences. Each was named only after it was seen:\n    - `views.created_at`, a wall-clock timestamp;\n    - `link_selections`, a table the current uncommitted store schema adds (D694), empty;\n    - `dependencies.kind`, a column the same schema adds, on a table empty in both.\n  - The design's named class was \"timestamps … and new empty tables\". The added column on an empty table is the same kind, but not\n    named in advance.\n  - T1 was then rerun in full into `citation-t1-2026-11-21-run2/`. It saved passing T1 and T1b results (`t1-result.json`,\n    `transport-log.json`), then exited 1: its summary print failed on a list value, a harness defect. The print is fixed, and the\n    current code exits 0 on the saved results. The saved data verifies the replay without repeating it (Codex r39 checked all 1,616\n    requests, the substitutions, the new hashes and the 36 tables).\n- **The first harness's store** is left in place, marked harness-only.\n- **Preflight** first let a refused judge row with neither a readable answer nor a saved format through with exit 0 (Codex r39,\n  reproduced). The format is now checked first; T5 covers the case, and its mutant is caught.\n- **Council round 39** (`codex-r39.md`): the build matches DESIGN v3; no v7 or v8 regression was found; T1's saved evidence holds;\n  T2 and T4 reproduce. The items above are its findings, all taken.\n\n## What the $0 test cannot show (DESIGN.md §6)\n\n- Whether the provider accepts the exact format: the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and the largest request.\n- How the provider counts a referenced enum.\n- Whether the judge, constrained, cites the intended source (e3111 could become e3110 or e3112).\n- Whether forecasts move.\n\nA paid step answers these, and it is Alex's to open. Its first part would send the largest stored request and an empty-list request\nto check acceptance. Then it would re-send the 17 stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones under v12, and read the\ncited sources beside the forecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '30,110p;170,307p;384,425p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '1,195p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/t2_offline.py | sed -n '1,155p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '30,110p;170,307p;384,425p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '1,195p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/t2_offline.py | sed -n '1,155p'\"","aggregated_output":"    30\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7', 'judging-v8', 'judging-v12')   # D354: the frozen judging prompt; D694: v8 = v7's text with the fuller dependency block; D712/D713: v12 = v7's text and request with closed id lists\n    31\tFULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK = ('judging-v8',)\n    32\tCLOSED_LISTS = ('judging-v12',)   # the answer's id fields take the ids the request lists (D713)\n    33\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\n    34\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\n    35\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\n    36\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\n    40\t    \"\"\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\"\"\"\n    41\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    42\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    46\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    47\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    48\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    49\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    50\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    51\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    52\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    53\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    54\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    55\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\tdef schema_for(prompt_version, lists=None):\n    59\t    \"\"\"The answer's format. Under judging-v12 (D713) its four id fields take the ids the request lists (`lists`, from\n    60\t    `request_parts`): one shared enum of the evidence ids for cites and push ids, the dependency ids for cites_views, the theme ids\n    61\t    for theme pushes; a field with no id allowed is an array with maxItems 0. Other versions ignore `lists`.\"\"\"\n    62\t    schema = _open_format(prompt_version)\n    63\t    if prompt_version not in CLOSED_LISTS:\n    64\t        return schema\n    65\t    if lists is None:\n    66\t        raise ValueError(f'{prompt_version} builds its answer format from the ids its request lists')\n    67\t    properties = schema['properties']\n    68\t    evidence, dependencies, themes = (sorted(set(lists[key])) for key in ('evidence', 'dependencies', 'themes'))\n    69\t    if evidence:\n    70\t        schema['$defs'] = {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence}}\n    71\t        properties['cites'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/evidence_id'}}\n    72\t        push_item = properties['pushes']['items']\n    73\t        properties['pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': dict(push_item, properties=dict(push_item['properties'], evidence_id={'$ref': '#/$defs/evidence_id'}))}\n    74\t    else:\n    75\t        properties['cites'] = dict(properties['cites'], maxItems=0)\n    76\t        properties['pushes'] = dict(properties['pushes'], maxItems=0)\n    77\t    if dependencies:\n    78\t        properties['cites_views'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': dependencies}}\n    79\t    else:\n    80\t        properties['cites_views'] = dict(properties['cites_views'], maxItems=0)\n    81\t    theme_item = properties['theme_pushes']['items']\n    82\t    if themes:\n    83\t        properties['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': dict(theme_item, properties=dict(theme_item['properties'], view_id={'type': 'string', 'enum': themes}))}\n    84\t    else:\n    85\t        properties['theme_pushes'] = dict(properties['theme_pushes'], maxItems=0)\n    86\t    return schema\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef _open_format(prompt_version):\n    90\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    91\t    pushes = PUSHES\n    92\t    schema = {\n    93\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    94\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n    95\t        'properties': {\n    96\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n    97\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n    98\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n    99\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n   100\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n   101\t        },\n   102\t    }\n   103\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n   104\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n   105\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n   106\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n   107\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n   108\t    return schema\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\n   173\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown. full_dependencies: the judging-v8 dependency block.\"\"\"\n   174\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   175\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   176\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   177\t    if hidden:\n   178\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   179\t    for p in pieces:\n   180\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   181\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   182\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   183\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   184\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   185\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   186\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   187\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   188\t    if deps:\n   189\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   190\t        for d in deps:\n   191\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   192\t            if not target:\n   193\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   194\t                continue\n   195\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   196\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   197\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   198\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   199\t            if full_dependencies:\n   200\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   203\t    if themes:\n   204\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   205\t        for theme in themes:\n   206\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   207\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   208\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   209\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   210\t    if last:\n   211\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   212\t    else:\n   213\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   214\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   215\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   216\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   217\t    return lines\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   221\t    system, user, _ = request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version)\n   222\t    return system, user\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   226\t    \"\"\"(system text, user text, the ids the request lists), all from the same rows at the same ledger state: the evidence pieces it\n   227\t    prints, the dependencies it gives an entry (resolved ones; a dependency still waiting has no id to cite) and the themes it prints.\"\"\"\n   228\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   229\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   230\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   231\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   232\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   233\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   234\t    themes = themes_in_force(conn, view_id)\n   235\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes, hidden=hidden,\n   236\t                           full_dependencies=prompt_version in FULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK)\n   237\t    lists = {'evidence': sorted({p['evidence_id'] for p in pieces}), 'dependencies': sorted({d['resolved_to'] for d in deps if d['resolved_to']}),\n   238\t             'themes': sorted({theme['view_id'] for theme in themes})}\n   239\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   240\t        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines), lists\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   244\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   248\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   249\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   250\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   254\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   255\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   256\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None, lists=None):\n   260\t    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n   261\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now. lists (judging-v12, D713): the ids the request\n   262\t    listed, from the rows that rendered it, the same lists its answer format closed; membership is checked against them.\"\"\"\n   263\t    errors = []\n   264\t    if lists is not None:\n   265\t        shown = set(lists['themes'])\n   266\t    else:\n   267\t        shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n   268\t    named = []\n   269\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n   270\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n   271\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n   272\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\n   273\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n   274\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n   275\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\n   276\t    if lists is not None:\n   277\t        allowed, deps = set(lists['evidence']), set(lists['dependencies'])\n   278\t    else:\n   279\t        allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\n   280\t        deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   281\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\n   282\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\n   283\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   284\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n   285\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   286\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   287\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   288\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   289\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   290\t        if cited not in deps:\n   291\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   292\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   293\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   294\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   295\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   296\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   297\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   298\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   299\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n   300\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n   301\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n   302\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n   303\t    return errors\n   304\t\n   305\t\n   306\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   307\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   384\t        if closed:                                         # D713: the format's lists and the check's lists come from the rows that render the text\n   385\t            parts = {v: request_parts(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   386\t            prompts = {v: parts[v][:2] for v in level}\n   387\t            lists = {v: parts[v][2] for v in level}\n   388\t            schemas = {v: schema_for(version, lists[v]) for v in level}\n   389\t        else:                                              # judging-v7/v8: through build_prompt, which harnesses wrap\n   390\t            prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   391\t            lists = {v: None for v in level}\n   392\t            schemas = {v: open_schema for v in level}\n   393\t\n   394\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   395\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   396\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schemas[view_id], 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   397\t\n   398\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   399\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   400\t        for view_id in level:\n   401\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   402\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1], lists[view_id])\n   403\t            if errors:\n   404\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   405\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   406\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1], lists[view_id])\n   407\t                if errors:\n   408\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   409\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   410\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   411\t            done.add(view_id)\n   412\t            results.append(result)\n   413\t            if result['changed']:\n   414\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   415\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   416\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   417\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n   418\t    return results\n     1\t\"\"\"One model call, archived and replayable.\n     2\t\n     3\t`call()` sends a system and user message with a strict JSON schema to an OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint (OpenAI,\n     4\tor DeepSeek through the same wire format), checks the answer against the schema, and records the exact request and\n     5\traw answer in an archive (SQLite, a POC artefact kept beside the test database, never inside the views database).\n     6\tA request whose sha256 is already in the archive is answered from it without a network call, so a rerun of a\n     7\treplay costs nothing and gives the same answers. The provider key is read from the owner-only credentials file and\n     8\tnever appears in the archive, logs or arguments.\n     9\t\"\"\"\n    10\timport dataclasses\n    11\timport base64\n    12\timport hashlib\n    13\timport http.client\n    14\timport json\n    15\timport re\n    16\timport os\n    17\timport sqlite3\n    18\timport time\n    19\timport uuid\n    20\timport urllib.error\n    21\timport urllib.request\n    22\t\n    23\tCREDENTIALS = os.path.expanduser('~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json')\n    24\tENDPOINTS = {'openai': ('https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions', 'OPENAI_API_KEY'),\n    25\t             'deepseek': ('https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions', 'DEEPSEEK_API_KEY')}\n    26\t# USD per million tokens, for the cost column only (an estimate; the provider's bill is the measurement)\n    27\t# gpt-6.1-sol: the published standard rates on 2026-11-16 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models: \"$2 / $10\" per million input and output\n    28\t# tokens; D628's model comparison only). gpt-6-astra: the published standard rates on 2026-11-16 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/\n    29\t# gpt-6-astra: \"$10 input … $50 output\" per million tokens; D632's comparison only).\n    30\t# claude-opus-5-5: Anthropic's first-party list price, $4 input and $20 output per million tokens (the claude-api skill's model table,\n    31\t# cached 2026-11-03); Alex's Opus trial only (2026-11-16, \"你试试看opus\"). Cache reads ($0.20) are priced at CACHED_INPUT_SHARE, an over-estimate.\n    32\t# gpt-6-luna: the published standard rates on 2026-10-25 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna: $0.10/M input, $0.50/M output,\n    33\t# cached input $0.01/M). Until this date the table carried (1.25, 10.0), so every cost_usd recorded before it is 12.5x (input) to 20x (output)\n    34\t# the published rate; the token columns are the measurement, the bill is the provider's.\n    35\tPRICES = {'gpt-6-luna': (0.10, 0.50), 'gpt-6.1-sol': (2.00, 10.00), 'gpt-6-astra': (10.00, 50.00), 'claude-opus-5-5': (4.00, 20.00), 'deepseek-flash': (0.30, 1.20), 'deepseek-v4-pro': (1.32, 3.96),\n    36\t          'jev-1.14.0': (0.042, 0.0)}   # Jev: docs.typesafe.ai/models, 2026-10-25; output free   # DeepSeek: peak-hour list prices, cache misses (2026-10-23 pricing page)\n    37\tCACHED_INPUT_SHARE = 0.10          # cached input tokens are priced at 10% of the input rate (gpt-6-luna page, read again 2026-10-27)\n    38\t\n    39\tSCHEMA_SQL = \"\"\"\n    40\tcreate table if not exists model_calls (\n    41\t  call_id integer primary key autoincrement, purpose text, config_version text, config_checksum text, model text,\n    42\t  request_sha256 text unique, request_json text, response_json text, answer_json text, prompt_chars integer,\n    43\t  input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text\n    44\t);\n    45\tcreate index if not exists model_calls_sha on model_calls(request_sha256);\n    46\t\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass SchemaError(ValueError):\n    50\t    pass\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tclass TransportError(RuntimeError):\n    54\t    pass\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    58\tclass Answer:\n    59\t    data: dict\n    60\t    call_id: int\n    61\t    request_sha256: str\n    62\t    cached: bool\n    63\t    prompt_chars: int\n    64\t    input_tokens: int\n    65\t    output_tokens: int\n    66\t    cost_usd: float\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n   103\t    def totals(self):\n   104\t        with self.lock:\n   105\t            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef _key(provider):\n   109\t    name = ENDPOINTS[provider][1]\n   110\t    if os.environ.get(name):\n   111\t        return os.environ[name]\n   112\t    with open(CREDENTIALS, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   113\t        return json.load(handle)[name]\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider):\n   117\t    request = {\n   118\t        'model': setting.model,\n   119\t        'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': system}, {'role': 'user', 'content': user}],\n   120\t        'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'name': schema_name, 'strict': True, 'schema': schema}},\n   121\t    }\n   122\t    if provider == 'openai':\n   123\t        request['max_completion_tokens'] = setting.max_output_tokens\n   124\t        if setting.reasoning_effort:\n   125\t            request['reasoning_effort'] = setting.reasoning_effort\n   126\t    else:\n   127\t        request['max_tokens'] = setting.max_output_tokens\n   128\t    return request\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\tdef openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the default preserves the production retry behavior\n   132\t    url, _ = ENDPOINTS[provider]\n   133\t    body = json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')\n   134\t    headers = {'Authorization': f'Bearer {_key(provider)}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\n   135\t    last = None\n   136\t    last_http = None\n   137\t    if isinstance(max_attempts, bool) or not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or max_attempts < 1:\n   138\t        raise ValueError('max_attempts must be a positive integer')\n   139\t    for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n   140\t        try:\n   141\t            with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=headers, method='POST'), timeout=timeout) as response:\n   142\t                raw_bytes = response.read()\n   143\t                try:\n   144\t                    raw = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8')\n   145\t                except UnicodeDecodeError:\n   146\t                    if max_attempts != 1:\n   147\t                        raise\n   148\t                    failure = TransportError('invalid UTF-8 HTTP response')\n   149\t                    failure.response_body = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace')\n   150\t                    failure.response_body_base64 = base64.b64encode(raw_bytes).decode('ascii')\n   151\t                    failure.http_status = response.status\n   152\t                    raise failure\n   153\t                try:\n   154\t                    return json.loads(raw)\n   155\t                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n   156\t                    if max_attempts != 1:\n   157\t                        raise\n   158\t                    failure = TransportError('malformed HTTP response')\n   159\t                    failure.response_body = raw\n   160\t                    failure.http_status = response.status\n   161\t                    raise failure\n   162\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n   163\t            body_bytes = error.read()\n   164\t            body_text = body_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace' if max_attempts == 1 else 'ignore')\n   165\t            last_http = (error.code, body_text, base64.b64encode(body_bytes).decode('ascii'))\n   166\t            last = f'HTTP {error.code}: {body_text[:600]}'\n   167\t            if error.code in (400, 401, 403, 404):\n   168\t                failure = TransportError(last)\n   169\t                failure.response_body = body_text\n   170\t                failure.response_body_base64 = last_http[2]\n   171\t                failure.http_status = error.code\n   172\t                raise failure\n   173\t        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ConnectionError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated response is retried like a network error\n   174\t            last = repr(error)[:200]\n   175\t            last_http = None   # the final failure describes the last attempt only\n   176\t        if max_attempts == 3 or attempt + 1 < max_attempts:\n   177\t            time.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   178\t    failure = TransportError(last or 'no answer')\n   179\t    if last_http:\n   180\t        failure.http_status, failure.response_body, failure.response_body_base64 = last_http\n   181\t    raise failure\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\tdef check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n   185\t    \"\"\"A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,\n   186\t    array/items/minItems/maxItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs.\"\"\"\n   187\t    root = root if root is not None else schema\n   188\t    if '$ref' in schema:\n   189\t        name = schema['$ref'].rsplit('/', 1)[1]\n   190\t        schema = root['$defs'][name]\n   191\t    kind = schema.get('type')\n   192\t    if 'anyOf' in schema:\n   193\t        # a value matching no option reports the closest options' errors (fewest), not merely the last option's\n   194\t        failures = []\n   195\t        for option in schema['anyOf']:\n     1\t\"\"\"T2 and T4 of the citation-only judge's $0 test (DESIGN.md §5; D713).\n     2\t\n     3\tT2 (evidence from the archived text): for every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3 and the two pilot arms' fresh rows, the\n     4\tclosed lists are taken from the request's text (evidence entries, dependency entries, theme entries), judging-v12's format is built\n     5\tfrom them, and the stored answer goes through the real `model.check_schema`. Pass: every committed answer and every valid uncommitted\n     6\tone validates; every refused answer fails on an id. The population is printed.\n     7\t\n     8\tT4: the largest format over those archives and over the sealed D358 archive: evidence ids, enum values with the shared evidence enum\n     9\tcounted once and counted per reference, and characters, against the provider's documented limits.\n    10\t\n    11\t  python3 t2_offline.py\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\timport json\n    14\timport re\n    15\timport sqlite3\n    16\timport sys\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\t\n    19\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    20\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    21\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    22\tfrom hivemind import model                                              # noqa: E402\n    23\tfrom hivemind.views import judging                                     # noqa: E402\n    24\t\n    25\tRUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    26\tPILOT_COPIES = Path('/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad')\n    27\tPILOT_TOP = 8737                                                        # the pilots' archives copy old-2's rows up to this call\n    28\tSOURCES = [('old-1', RUN / 'old-1/prod', 0), ('old-2', RUN / 'old-2/prod', 0), ('old-3', RUN / 'old-3/prod', 0),\n    29\t           ('control-1', PILOT_COPIES / 'control-1-copy', PILOT_TOP), ('linked-1', PILOT_COPIES / 'linked-1-copy', PILOT_TOP)]\n    30\tSEALED = REPO / 'poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite'\n    31\tPUSH_ENUM_VALUES = 6                                                    # the two existing 3-value push enums\n    32\tPROVIDER_ENUM_LIMIT = 1000\n    33\tRETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: '\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef dependencies_shown_in(user):\n    37\t    block = user.split('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]', 1)\n    38\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef lists_from_text(user):\n    42\t    return {'evidence': sorted(judging.evidence_shown_in(user)), 'dependencies': sorted(dependencies_shown_in(user)),\n    43\t            'themes': sorted(judging.themes_shown_in(user))}\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\tdef size(lists, schema):\n    47\t    e, d, t = len(lists['evidence']), len(lists['dependencies']), len(lists['themes'])\n    48\t    return {'evidence': e, 'enum values, shared enum counted once': e + d + t + PUSH_ENUM_VALUES,\n    49\t            'enum values, counted per reference': 2 * e + d + t + PUSH_ENUM_VALUES, 'format chars': len(json.dumps(schema))}\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef t2():\n    53\t    population = {'archive rows': 0, 'distinct request-answer pairs': 0, 'committed': 0, 'refused': 0, 'valid uncommitted': 0}\n    54\t    failures, refused_detail, seen, sizes, open_chars = [], [], set(), [], []\n    55\t    open_format_chars = len(json.dumps(judging.schema_for('judging-v7')))\n    56\t    for label, folder, top in SOURCES:\n    57\t        archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    58\t        views = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    59\t        committed_calls = {r[0] for r in views.execute('select call_id from judgements')}\n    60\t        for call_id, sha, request_json, answer_json in archive.execute(\n    61\t                \"select call_id, request_sha256, request_json, answer_json from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id>? order by call_id\", (top,)):\n    62\t            population['archive rows'] += 1\n    63\t            request = json.loads(request_json)\n    64\t            user = request['messages'][1]['content']\n    65\t            pair = (sha.split(':')[0], answer_json)\n    66\t            if pair in seen:\n    67\t                continue\n    68\t            seen.add(pair)\n    69\t            population['distinct request-answer pairs'] += 1\n    70\t            lists = lists_from_text(user.split(RETRY_MARK, 1)[0])        # a retry carries the first request's text, then the note\n    71\t            schema = judging.schema_for('judging-v12', lists)\n    72\t            sizes.append(size(lists, schema))\n    73\t            errors = model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), schema)\n    74\t            refused = ':refused:' in sha or ':schema:' in sha\n    75\t            if refused:\n    76\t                population['refused'] += 1\n    77\t                refused_detail.append({'source': label, 'call': call_id, 'format errors': errors[:3]})\n    78\t                if not errors:\n    79\t                    failures.append({'source': label, 'call': call_id, 'why': 'a refused answer passes the closed format'})\n    80\t            else:\n    81\t                population['committed' if call_id in committed_calls else 'valid uncommitted'] += 1\n    82\t                if errors:\n    83\t                    failures.append({'source': label, 'call': call_id, 'why': errors[:3]})\n    84\t    chars = sorted(s['format chars'] for s in sizes)\n    85\t    return {'population': population, 'T2 failures': failures, 'refused answers and their format errors': refused_detail,\n    86\t            'T2 pass': not failures and population['refused'] > 0,\n    87\t            'format chars': {'judging-v7': open_format_chars, 'v12 median': chars[len(chars) // 2], 'v12 max': chars[-1]},\n    88\t            'largest (T4)': max(sizes, key=lambda s: s['evidence'])}\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\tdef t4_sealed():\n    92\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{SEALED}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    93\t    sizes = []\n    94\t    for (request_json,) in archive.execute(\"select request_json from model_calls where purpose='judge'\"):\n    95\t        user = json.loads(request_json)['messages'][1]['content']\n    96\t        lists = lists_from_text(user)\n    97\t        sizes.append(size(lists, judging.schema_for('judging-v12', lists)))\n    98\t    over_once = sum(s['enum values, shared enum counted once'] > PROVIDER_ENUM_LIMIT for s in sizes)\n    99\t    over_twice = sum(s['enum values, counted per reference'] > PROVIDER_ENUM_LIMIT for s in sizes)\n   100\t    return {'requests': len(sizes), 'largest': max(sizes, key=lambda s: s['evidence']),\n   101\t            f'over {PROVIDER_ENUM_LIMIT} with the shared enum counted once': over_once,\n   102\t            f'over {PROVIDER_ENUM_LIMIT} counted per reference': over_twice}\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\tdef main():\n   106\t    result = t2()\n   107\t    result['T4 sealed D358 archive'] = t4_sealed()\n   108\t    (HERE / 't2-result.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   109\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in result.items() if k != 'refused answers and their format errors'}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   110\t    for row in result['refused answers and their format errors']:\n   111\t        print(row['source'], row['call'], row['format errors'][:1])\n   112\t    sys.exit(0 if result['T2 pass'] else 1)\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   116\t    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D715|D714|One next task' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n '\"'^## D358|''^## D71[0-5]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D715|D714|One next task' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n '\"'^## D358|''^## D71[0-5]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,135p'\"","aggregated_output":"77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n126:**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \"null\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\n159:## One next task\n448:**The one next task (D714, 2026-11-21): Alex's choice on the paid acceptance step for judging-v12.** The step: the largest stored\n454:- **Passed every registered $0 check** (D714; `research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md`):\n902:  numbers) was answered by him on 2026-11-15 (D505; see \"One next task\").\n904:  published rates); the current figure is in \"One next task\". (An earlier line here gave \"about $29.2\" as tracked spend; no decision or\n3783:## D358 · 2026-10-28 (carried 2026-11-04) · The three-month run stops at 2026-08-28 and is sealed; evidence bloat is the next problem to solve\n10652:## D710 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $2.50 ceiling for the pilot; pair 1 is sent\n10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n10699:## D713 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes); build judging-v12 and poc-v121 with the $0 test\n10721:## D714 · 2026-11-21 · judging-v12 and poc-v121 built; every registered $0 check passes; the paid acceptance step is Alex's\n10756:## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n     1\t# Paid acceptance probe of judging-v12 (design, D715; registered before any send)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Alex's ceiling:** $0.50 (D715, \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"), held by a reservation ledger (`budget_replay.SharedLedger`) that stops at it.\n     4\t**Plan file:** `probe-plan.json` (`probe_plan.py`, $0). **Model and settings:** poc-v121's rejudging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium\n     5\teffort, 16,000 output tokens), the provider's strict format.\n     6\t\n     7\t## 1. What it decides\n     8\t\n     9\t| Question | How it is answered |\n    10\t|---|---|\n    11\t| Q1. Does the provider accept judging-v12's format on a real request, the largest one included? | Part A |\n    12\t| Q2. On the requests the open format let the model get wrong, does it now cite the intended source, or put a wrong but listed id in its place? | Part B |\n    13\t| Q3. On ordinary requests, does the closed format change what the judge cites or concludes, beyond its own variation under the open format? | Part C |\n    14\t\n    15\tPart A also records whether the provider counts a referenced enum once. That decides whether three-month runs fit; it is not a gate.\n    16\t\n    17\t## 2. The sends\n    18\t\n    19\tEach request is sent with its stored system and user text, unchanged.\n    20\t\n    21\t- **Part A, acceptance, 2 sends.**\n    22\t  - (A1) the largest stored request of the five archives: old-1 call 5652, 451 evidence ids; 464 enum values counted once, 915 per\n    23\t    reference;\n    24\t  - (A2) the sealed D358 run's largest: call 6918, 647 ids; 676 counted once, 1,323 per reference.\n    25\t  - Every request also carries `cites_views` with `maxItems: 0` (no dependency in poc-v118), so Part A exercises the empty-list form.\n    26\t  - A2 is a format check on an older request text (poc-v34's judge request with v12's format built from its lists). Its answer is\n    27\t    not read.\n    28\t- **Part B, the refused requests: 16 distinct, 3 sends each, under v12's format.**\n    29\t  - 17 refused rows give 16 distinct requests: control-1's 8941 is 8938's retry (the same request plus the note).\n    30\t  - linked-1's 7 requests carry judging-v8's dependency block. They are sent with v12's builder's format for their lists, a format\n    31\t    probe on the stored text. No v8-based version exists or is built.\n    32\t- **Part C, matched ordinary requests: 16 distinct, 3 sends under v12's format and 3 under judging-v7's open format** (the fresh\n    33\t  control). Each matched request is the same question's accepted first-attempt request in the same archive with the closest evidence\n    34\t  count (`probe_plan.py`).\n    35\t- **Order:** A, then B, then C with each request's v12 and v7 sends together and the cheapest requests first. A ceiling stop leaves\n    36\t  only complete pairs, and the report says which requests were not reached.\n    37\t- **Estimate** (stored tokens at the published rates): about $0.43. Actual output tokens vary; the ledger stops at $0.50.\n    38\t- **One send at a time per request,** a thread pool of 4 across requests.\n    39\t- **A transport or provider error** is recorded and not retried beyond the transport's own policy. An HTTP 400 is the Part A\n    40\t  finding.\n    41\t\n    42\t## 3. Reading rule (frozen before the send)\n    43\t\n    44\t### Part A\n    45\tQ1 passes when A1 returns HTTP 200 with an answer that passes the format and `check_answer` against its lists. For A2, a 200 means\n    46\ta referenced enum counts once (or the provider tolerates 1,323); a 400 is recorded with its body.\n    47\t\n    48\t### Part B\n    49\tEach of the 48 answers is read by hand beside its request.\n    50\t- **The fact.** First, before any answer is read, the original refused answer is read: for each bad id, the fact its reasons or push\n    51\t  attach to it, and the request's entry that carries that fact (by quote), or \"ambiguous\" when two entries could. These are the\n    52\t  intended targets, written to `probe-targets.json`.\n    53\t- **Evidence-id cases** (e88, e3955, e3998, e1382, e2769, e393, e362/e3111, e693). Each answer is classed for each target:\n    54\t  - *intended*: it cites the entry that carries the fact;\n    55\t  - *dropped*: no listed entry is cited for that fact;\n    56\t  - *misattributed*: it cites a listed entry for that fact whose quote does not carry it;\n    57\t  - *unclear*: the answer no longer states the fact. That counts as dropped and is reported apart.\n    58\t- **Placement cases** (theme ids in cites or `cites_views`; the dependency v14 as evidence). *Correct*: the theme appears only in\n    59\t  `theme_pushes`, or the dependency only in `cites_views`. *Absent*: it is not named.\n    60\t- **Every answer:** passes `check_answer` (a refusal is counted); its rung and implied outcome are set beside the stored accepted\n    61\t  retry's.\n    62\t- A second, blind reader (Codex) reads the same 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read.\n    63\t\n    64\t### Part C\n    65\tPer request: the rungs of the 3 v12 and the 3 v7 answers, and each answer's cited set against the stored answer's (the share of\n    66\tthe stored cites kept). A format effect is flagged when:\n    67\t- the v12 rungs fall outside the range of the v7 rungs and the stored rung; or\n    68\t- v12's mean share of kept cites is below v7's by more than v7's own spread (its max minus its min).\n    69\t\n    70\tEvery flagged request is read by hand: is a source dropped or changed, and why?\n    71\t\n    72\t### Outcome (registered)\n    73\t- **Ready to adopt** (to propose to Alex as the product's judge format), when all hold:\n    74\t  - Q1 passes;\n    75\t  - in Part B no answer is refused and misattributed answers are at most 2 of 48;\n    76\t  - in Part C no flagged request shows a source wrongly dropped or replaced because of the format.\n    77\t- **Not ready**, with its reason:\n    78\t  - Q1 fails;\n    79\t  - more than 2 misattributions;\n    80\t  - a Part B refusal;\n    81\t  - a Part C format effect confirmed by reading.\n    82\t\n    83\tUnclear or ambiguous cases are reported and do not count for or against. Both outcomes go to Alex; adoption itself is his decision.\n    84\t\n    85\t### Why 2 of 48\n    86\tThe open format turned these same requests into refusals 17 of 17 times. Under the closed format a misattribution passes silently,\n    87\tso it is the harm to bound. Two in 48 (about 4%) is the order of the original slips' rate on these hardest requests. A higher rate\n    88\twould trade a visible refusal for a silent wrong citation too often.\n    89\t\n    90\t## 4. Harness and $0 proof before the send\n    91\t\n    92\t`probe.py`, harness-only:\n    93\t- it reads `probe-plan.json`, builds each request with `model.build_request` from poc-v121's setting and v12's format (or v7's), and\n    94\t  sends through `budget_replay.BudgetTransport` on a ledger at $0.50;\n    95\t- each answer goes through `model.check_schema` and `judging.check_answer` (with the lists);\n    96\t- answers are written to `probe-answers.jsonl` with the request's sha, part, send number and cost.\n    97\t\n    98\tBefore the send, at $0:\n    99\t- a dry run with a fake transport answering stored answers checks that every request is built as planned: the system and user text\n   100\t  equal the stored ones; the format equals `schema_for('judging-v12', lists)`, or v7's for the control;\n   101\t- the ledger refuses a ceiling other than $0.50;\n   102\t- a mutant (a request sent with the open format in Part B) is caught by the dry check.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
