{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/round40-brief.md; ls -l docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/*r40*; sed -n '140,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Council round 40: the paid acceptance probe of judging-v12, design review (read-only)\n\nAlex approved $0.50 for a paid acceptance step of the citation-only judge (D715; his words in `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` D715). Review\n`docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md` before any harness is written. Context: `DESIGN.md`, `RESULT.md`,\n`probe_plan.py` and its output `probe-plan.json` (the planned requests), `src/hivemind/views/judging.py`, `src/hivemind/model.py`,\n`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py` (the ledger). Out of scope: the frozen ruler, the prompt text, the link direction,\nother modules. No paid call.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Does each part answer its question, and is the reading rule exact enough to apply blind (targets frozen before answers are read;\n   the classes; the Part C flag)? Find a case it misclassifies or a way it could pass while the format is harmful.\n2. Is the outcome rule right (Q1; at most 2 misattributions of 48; no refusal; no confirmed Part C effect)? Is 2 of 48 defensible, or\n   should it be stated differently?\n3. Is the plan right: 16 distinct refused requests (8941 is 8938's retry), linked-1's v8-shaped requests sent with v12's builder's format,\n   the matched requests, the fresh v7 control, the sealed request as a counting check, the order and the cost (about $0.43 of $0.50)? Is\n   anything worth dropping to protect the margin, or missing?\n4. The $0 proof before the send: enough?\nAnswer READY TO BUILD THE HARNESS or NOT READY with the blocking items.\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 22 00:27 docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/codex-r40.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  359829 Nov 22 00:28 docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/codex-r40.stream\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_plan.py; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '219,308p'; sed -n '3783,3808p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '10660,10699p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"$0: the paid acceptance probe's request plan (PROBE-DESIGN.md; D715). Writes probe-plan.json:\n     2\t\n     3\t- acceptance: the largest stored request of the five archives (most evidence ids), and the sealed D358 run's largest (647 ids; its\n     4\t  shared evidence enum is under the documented 1,000 values only if a referenced enum counts once);\n     5\t- refused: the 17 distinct stored refused judge requests (old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1 fresh rows), each with its bad ids;\n     6\t- matched: for each refused request, the same question's accepted first-attempt request in the same archive whose evidence count is\n     7\t  closest (ties: the nearest earlier call), never a request of the refused set.\n     8\t\n     9\tEach entry carries the stored system and user texts, the closed lists read from the text, and a cost estimate from the stored tokens at\n    10\tthe published gpt-6-luna rates.\n    11\t\n    12\t  python3 probe_plan.py\n    13\t\"\"\"\n    14\timport json\n    15\timport re\n    16\timport sqlite3\n    17\timport sys\n    18\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    19\t\n    20\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    21\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    22\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    23\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    24\tfrom hivemind import model                                              # noqa: E402\n    25\tfrom hivemind.views import judging                                     # noqa: E402\n    26\timport t2_offline                                                       # noqa: E402\n    27\t\n    28\tPRICE_IN, PRICE_OUT = model.PRICES['gpt-6-luna']\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef view_of(user):\n    32\t    match = re.match(r'Thesis (v\\d+) \\(', user)\n    33\t    return match.group(1) if match else None\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef cost(tokens_in, tokens_out):\n    37\t    return round((tokens_in or 0) / 1e6 * PRICE_IN + (tokens_out or 0) / 1e6 * PRICE_OUT, 6)\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\tdef entry(label, call_id, request, tokens_in, tokens_out, answer_json=None):\n    41\t    user = request['messages'][1]['content'].split(t2_offline.RETRY_MARK, 1)[0]\n    42\t    lists = t2_offline.lists_from_text(user)\n    43\t    return {'source': label, 'call_id': call_id, 'view': view_of(user), 'system': request['messages'][0]['content'], 'user': user,\n    44\t            'lists': lists, 'evidence count': len(lists['evidence']), 'stored answer': answer_json,\n    45\t            'estimated cost': cost(tokens_in, tokens_out), 'stored tokens': [tokens_in, tokens_out]}\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\tdef main():\n    49\t    refused, accepted_by_source, largest = [], {}, None\n    50\t    seen = set()\n    51\t    for label, folder, top in t2_offline.SOURCES:\n    52\t        archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    53\t        views = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    54\t        committed = {r[0] for r in views.execute('select call_id from judgements')}\n    55\t        for call_id, sha, request_json, answer_json, tokens_in, tokens_out in archive.execute(\n    56\t                \"select call_id, request_sha256, request_json, answer_json, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls \"\n    57\t                \"where purpose='judge' and call_id>? order by call_id\", (top,)):\n    58\t            request = json.loads(request_json)\n    59\t            pair = (sha.split(':')[0], answer_json)\n    60\t            if pair in seen:\n    61\t                continue\n    62\t            seen.add(pair)\n    63\t            item = entry(label, call_id, request, tokens_in, tokens_out, answer_json)\n    64\t            if largest is None or item['evidence count'] > largest['evidence count']:\n    65\t                largest = item\n    66\t            if ':refused:' in sha:\n    67\t                schema = judging.schema_for('judging-v12', item['lists'])\n    68\t                item['bad ids'] = sorted({re.search(r\"'([^']+)' not in\", e).group(1) for e in model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), schema)\n    69\t                                          if \"' not in\" in e})\n    70\t                refused.append(item)\n    71\t            elif call_id in committed and t2_offline.RETRY_MARK not in request['messages'][1]['content']:\n    72\t                accepted_by_source.setdefault(label, []).append(item)\n    73\t    distinct = {}\n    74\t    for item in refused:                           # a retry carries its first request's text: one request, the bad ids of both attempts\n    75\t        key = (item['source'], item['user'])\n    76\t        if key in distinct:\n    77\t            distinct[key]['bad ids'] = sorted(set(distinct[key]['bad ids']) | set(item['bad ids']))\n    78\t            distinct[key]['refused calls'].append(item['call_id'])\n    79\t        else:\n    80\t            distinct[key] = dict(item, **{'refused calls': [item['call_id']]})\n    81\t    refused = list(distinct.values())\n    82\t    refused_users = set(distinct)\n    83\t    matched = []\n    84\t    for item in refused:\n    85\t        pool = [a for a in accepted_by_source.get(item['source'], []) if a['view'] == item['view'] and (a['source'], a['user']) not in refused_users]\n    86\t        if not pool:\n    87\t            raise SystemExit(f'{item[\"source\"]} {item[\"call_id\"]}: no accepted request of {item[\"view\"]} to match')\n    88\t        best = min(pool, key=lambda a: (abs(a['evidence count'] - item['evidence count']), abs(a['call_id'] - item['call_id'])))\n    89\t        matched.append(dict(best, matches=f'{item[\"source\"]}:{item[\"call_id\"]}'))\n    90\t    sealed = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{t2_offline.SEALED}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    91\t    sealed_largest = None\n    92\t    for call_id, request_json, tokens_in, tokens_out in sealed.execute(\"select call_id, request_json, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where purpose='judge'\"):\n    93\t        item = entry('sealed-D358', call_id, json.loads(request_json), tokens_in, tokens_out)\n    94\t        if sealed_largest is None or item['evidence count'] > sealed_largest['evidence count']:\n    95\t            sealed_largest = item\n    96\t    plan = {'acceptance': [largest, sealed_largest], 'refused': refused, 'matched': matched}\n    97\t    sends = {'acceptance': 1, 'refused': 3, 'matched under v12': 3, 'matched under v7 (control)': 3}\n    98\t    estimate = (sum(a['estimated cost'] for a in plan['acceptance']) + 3 * sum(r['estimated cost'] for r in refused)\n    99\t                + 6 * sum(m['estimated cost'] for m in matched))\n   100\t    plan['sends'], plan['estimate'] = sends, round(estimate, 4)\n   101\t    (HERE / 'probe-plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(plan, ensure_ascii=False))\n   102\t    print(json.dumps({'acceptance': [(a['source'], a['call_id'], a['evidence count'], a['estimated cost']) for a in plan['acceptance']],\n   103\t                      'refused': [(r['source'], r['call_id'], r['view'], r['evidence count'], r['bad ids']) for r in refused],\n   104\t                      'matched': [(m['source'], m['call_id'], m['view'], m['evidence count'], m['matches']) for m in matched],\n   105\t                      'sends': sends, 'estimate (stored tokens, published rates)': plan['estimate']}, indent=1))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   109\t    main()\n   219\t            return [f'{path}: expected array']\n   220\t        errors = []\n   221\t        if len(value) < schema.get('minItems', 0):\n   222\t            errors.append(f'{path}: fewer than {schema[\"minItems\"]} items')\n   223\t        if 'maxItems' in schema and len(value) > schema['maxItems']:\n   224\t            errors.append(f'{path}: more than {schema[\"maxItems\"]} items')\n   225\t        for index, item in enumerate(value):\n   226\t            errors.extend(check_schema(item, schema.get('items', {}), f'{path}[{index}]', root))\n   227\t        return errors\n   228\t    if kind == 'string':\n   229\t        if not isinstance(value, str):\n   230\t            return [f'{path}: expected string']\n   231\t        if 'enum' in schema and value not in schema['enum']:\n   232\t            return [f'{path}: {value!r} not in {schema[\"enum\"]}']\n   233\t        if 'pattern' in schema and not re.search(schema['pattern'], value):\n   234\t            return [f'{path}: {value!r} does not match {schema[\"pattern\"]}']\n   235\t        return []\n   236\t    if kind == 'integer':\n   237\t        return [] if isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected integer']\n   238\t    if kind == 'number':\n   239\t        return [] if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected number']\n   240\t    if kind == 'boolean':\n   241\t        return [] if isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected boolean']\n   242\t    if kind == 'null':\n   243\t        return [] if value is None else [f'{path}: expected null']\n   244\t    return []\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\tdef request_identity(request):\n   248\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   249\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   250\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   254\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   255\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   256\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   257\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   258\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   259\t    if hit:\n   260\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   261\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   262\t    started = time.time()\n   263\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   264\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   265\t    try:\n   266\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   267\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   268\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   269\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   270\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   271\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   272\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   273\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   274\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   275\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   276\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   277\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   278\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   279\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   280\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   281\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   282\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   283\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   284\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   285\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   286\t    if errors:\n   287\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   288\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n## D358 · 2026-10-28 (carried 2026-11-04) · The three-month run stops at 2026-08-28 and is sealed; evidence bloat is the next problem to solve\n\nRecorded on 2026-10-28 as D206 of `feat/thesis-admission-v12` in that worktree's uncommitted decision log, and never merged; carried into\n`main` on 2026-11-04 when the worktree was removed (D359), its text unchanged below. Its D206 is a different decision on `main`.\nIts quality review is carried as `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/` (documents and scripts; the comparison databases stay in\nthe backup). The writer fix it names was not carried: `main` reads cited ids as a set where it serves them (`bundle.library`,\n`service`), which covers the same defect. The succession gap it records was not checked against today's code.\n\n- Alex, 16:30: \"你先停止吧，把这个db 封存，替换成最新的FE可以读取然后把这个 bloating evidence 的问题给记录下来，很严重，需要解决\". Earlier (16:12): \"证据膨胀是一个问题，我们之后要想办法deal\".\n- The run (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, poc-v34, the D202–D205 writer) completed 59 days, 2026-07-01 to 08-28: 1,232 items, 69 theses, 7,091 calls, $5.80. It is sealed read-only as `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/` (SQLite online backups, SHA256SUMS, logs and scripts; the run folder is left resumable). The front end reads it from 16:35: the served defaults switched in the five places the README names (main checkout), `poc/mock/index.html` rebuilt, the API restarted in `service-3m-2026-10-28/` (`/days` 2026-07-01..08-28, 69 theses).\n- Why it stops: evidence bloat. The Data Center revenue thesis (v10) carried 1,768 linked pieces by 08-27 and FY2027 revenue (v2) 1,733; v10's judging request was 292 KB with 698 evidence ids shown; the model mislabels one id among dozens of pushes about every other attempt, the code refuses the answer, two refusals halt the day. Today: 14 judge answers refused by code, 10 on v10/v2/v13, two days halted on v10 alone in 16:05–16:21. Of 25 pieces linked to v2, 10 bear on the question (Claude's reading); the judge ever cited 23–27% of what is linked. The census, the one-case traces and the rule candidates are in `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/report.md` §2 D (and A–C, measured first); the step is Alex's to pick.\n- Found while switching the front end: one judgement (v2, id 736) cited an id twice and the UI contract (`thesis-ui/2`, uniqueItems) refused the dataset. The writer now stores each cited id once (`judging._record`, test `test_a_judgement_stores_each_cited_id_once`, red on the old writer); the two readers of sealed ledgers (`bundle.library`, `service` thesis bundles, main checkout) read the set, since a sealed ledger does not change.\n- The other halts of the day, each resumed by the run's `watch.sh` and recorded in the cost ledger: the judging output cap (D205), the Mac sleeping, three transport errors, one \"database is locked\" (a reader held the ledger over the 5 s busy timeout), one hung call (55 min at 0% CPU under the VPN; a stall detector was added to the watcher).\n- Amendment, 17:05. Alex, on seeing an empty thesis in the front end (\"why is this here? there is no evidence and why is this a thesis\"; then \"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\"): v68, \"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\", opened on the run's last day by the succession rule (D168: same quantity, next period, after v24) from one statement (\"$20 billion in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027\"); the writer linked that statement to v7 and v24 (as a repeat of the $20 billion piece) and not to the successor it opened, so v68 stood with no evidence and, judging running only on arrivals, no judgement. Class: 1 of 69 theses with no evidence; 1 of 2 successions (v9 after v8 has 59 pieces). The sealed folder stays untouched; the front end, the API and the page build now read `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite`, the same ledger with v68's rows removed (views, view_keys, rungs, successions, view_switches, views_fts; the append-only triggers dropped in that copy only; its README lists this). The writer gap (a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the successor) is an open defect in `writing.py` for the next slice.\n\n## D359 · 2026-11-04 · The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight reads the one-decider requests\n\n- Alex, on Claude's list of the two open cleanup items (the old worktrees, and the code paths only retired prompt versions take, with the\n  cost that old versions could then no longer be re-run, only read from their stored results): \"你看完你告诉我呀\", then \"ok\".\n- **Worktrees.** Removed: `fix/thesis-admission-v11` (its 102 MB of data were five SQLite files whose contents equal `main`'s; only the\n  header counters differed), `cleanup/sequential-requests` (685 MB, 244 files byte-identical to `main`'s `poc/data`), `feat/parallel-day`\n  (two text changes `main` already holds, 94 MB of the 2026-10-25/26 test outputs) and `feat/thesis-admission-v12` (a writer fix `main`\n  covers where it reads, the sealed-run decision carried as D358, its quality review carried to `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/`).\n  What was kept from each is in `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-backups/old-worktrees-2026-11-04/` (README there); the branches stay. Kept:\n  `fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28`, whose ignored folders hold the stored end-to-end runs (679 MB; v91, v92, v94, v95), the results\n  any later comparison reads.\n## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21, on the stopped control): \"好你跑一次council 看trace 同意了就开始下一步\".\n- **Registered verdict:** inconclusive. control-1 (poc-v118) stopped on 09-08 when v21's answer and its retry each cited an id outside\n  the listed evidence (`e362` for `e3620`; `e3111` beside `e3110`/`e3112`), PAID-DESIGN.md §4 (2). linked-1 completed with every\n  acceptance check true. control-1 equals old-2 on every H2 table through 09-07. Spend $1.70 of $2.50.\n- **Exploratory, one pair, one draw, beside the verdict** (`whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md`):\n  - P: the parser counts 3 of 60 dates (linked-1) against 28 of 60 (control-1) on 07-10..09-07. All 12 flagged linked dates were read:\n    none has Data Center above total revenue (parser artefacts). The 5 sampled control dates are real.\n  - H4: four linked v14 answers (07-15..07-18) add v8's stand-alone CPU forecast to a total built from company guidance, read by Claude\n    and, shuffled, by Codex.\n  - H1: 5 linked against 1 control refusal on the 200 matched reader-days, at the harm line.\n  - Every refused judge answer seen is an id-membership error: 17 in 5,408 distinct attempts. 6 of linked-1's 7 fresh reader refusals\n    put an id in the wrong list, though the request's closing instruction forbids it.\n- **Council round 37** (`round37-brief.md`, `codex-r37.md`, `claude-r37.md`, `round37b-brief.md`, `codex-r37b.md`), consensus A:\n  - pair 1 is closed, with no redraw (B) and no resume (C);\n  - C would move H1 across its line through the refusals that invalidated the control, and its rule was proposed after the stop was\n    seen;\n  - Claude proposed C first and withdrew it on linked-1's H1 numbers;\n  - a resume-once rule may be registered only for a future comparison, before its send, in both arms, and proven on stored data.\n- **Recommendation to Alex (his to open, a new version of the frozen judge):**\n  - The version: a judge version that changes the citation format only. Every id field (cites, push ids, `cites_views`, theme\n    pushes) takes a closed list built from the exact request.\n  - The test, at $0, end to end: stored accepted answers fit; observed bad ids are excluded; an empty list is the only answer for a\n    field with no allowed id.\n  - A separate design, not part of this version: the link direction (a whole reading its own part). The keys label stand-alone CPU\n    `other`, and the direction is a judgement, which D704 left open on purpose.\n- **Not done:** no paid call after the pilot, no product file changed.\n\n## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n\n- **The question:** \"试点到此收尾（结论\"说不准\"，花了 1.70 美元）。发现了两个问题：一是模型常写出不在名单上的编号，回答因此被退回，这次对照组就是因为这个停下；二是新版本让\"总收入\"把 CPU 收入又加了一遍。下一步做哪个？\"\n  Options: 开引用格式新版本 (recommended: every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; $0 check on\n  stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; asking again before any paid test); 先设计重复计算的修法;\n  先停在这里.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\".\n- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n  a separate design. Design, then council review, then build with tests and mutants, then the $0 test; any paid test asks Alex again.\n\n## D713 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes); build judging-v12 and poc-v121 with the $0 test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys, json, collections\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\nhere=Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists'\\\\'').resolve()\nsys.path[:0]=[str(here), str(Path('\\\\''src'\\\\'').resolve()),str(Path('\\\\''clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13'\\\\'').resolve())]\nfrom hivemind import model\nfrom hivemind.views import judging\nimport budget_replay\nplan=json.loads((here/'\\\\''probe-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nprint('\\\\''keys'\\\\'',list(plan),'\\\\''estimate'\\\\'',plan.get('\\\\''estimate'\\\\''))\ntotals=collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor arm in ('\\\\''acceptance'\\\\'','\\\\''refused'\\\\'','\\\\''matched'\\\\''):\n    print(arm,len(plan[arm]),len(set((r['\\\\''system'\\\\''],r['\\\\''user'\\\\'']) for r in plan[arm])))\n    for r in plan[arm]:\n        print(r['\\\\''source'\\\\''],r['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],r['\\\\''view'\\\\''],[len(r['\\\\''lists'\\\\''][k]) for k in ('\\\\''evidence'\\\\'','\\\\''dependencies'\\\\'','\\\\''themes'\\\\'')],r.get('\\\\''refused calls'\\\\''),r.get('\\\\''bad ids'\\\\''),r.get('\\\\''matches'\\\\''),r['\\\\''estimated cost'\\\\''],list(set(r)-{'\\\\''source'\\\\'','\\\\''call_id'\\\\'','\\\\''view'\\\\'','\\\\''system'\\\\'','\\\\''user'\\\\'','\\\\''lists'\\\\'','\\\\''evidence count'\\\\'','\\\\''stored answer'\\\\'','\\\\''estimated cost'\\\\'','\\\\''stored tokens'\\\\'','\\\\''bad ids'\\\\'','\\\\''refused calls'\\\\'','\\\\''matches'\\\\''}))\n        for version in (['\\\\''judging-v12'\\\\'','\\\\''judging-v7'\\\\''] if arm=='\\\\''matched'\\\\'' else ['\\\\''judging-v12'\\\\'']):\n            rq=model.build_request(SimpleNamespace(model='\\\\''gpt-6-luna'\\\\'',max_output_tokens=16000,reasoning_effort='\\\\''medium'\\\\''),r['\\\\''system'\\\\''],r['\\\\''user'\\\\''],judging.schema_for(version,r['\\\\''lists'\\\\'']),'\\\\''judgement'\\\\'','\\\\''openai'\\\\'')\n            totals[arm].extend([(budget_replay.llm_estimate(rq),r['\\\\''estimated cost'\\\\''])]*(1 if arm=='\\\\''acceptance'\\\\'' else 3))\n    data=totals[arm]\n    print('\\\\''reservations min max sum; archived cost sum'\\\\'',min(x[0] for x in data),max(x[0] for x in data),sum(x[0] for x in data),sum(x[1] for x in data))\nprint('\\\\''sum'\\\\'',sum(x[1] for arr in totals.values() for x in arr),'\\\\''sum reservations'\\\\'',sum(x[0] for arr in totals.values() for x in arr))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
