{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The probe could pass even if judging-v12 drops the 85.4% growth estimate and its citation in all three answers. The current rule would record three omissions, zero wrong citations, and allow adoption. The budget rules also allow the run to stop halfway through a comparison that the design promises to finish. [Probe design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:35)\n\n1. **Make the reading rules usable blind.** In Part B, freeze the fact, the correct source or acceptable equivalents, the citation’s role, and the supporting passage for every bad citation in **both** saved attempts. `control-1:8938` gives a clear target for `e362`: `e3620` contains the 85.4% estimate. Its retry, `8941`, cites `e3111` for a generic downside discussion. The two nearby entries describe different risks, so their numbering alone cannot settle the target. The plan keeps both bad IDs but only the first answer, and there is no accepted retry for this request. Distinguish an omitted material fact from a fact stated without support. If an answer gives both a correct source and a wrong source for the same fact, count the wrong attribution. For misplaced theme and dependency citations, also check whether the answer silently substitutes another source. [Plan builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_plan.py:66) · [Pilot record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10660)\n\n   In Part C, read all 16 comparisons blind and use the numeric flags to prioritize the reading. For example, suppose the saved answer and all three fresh controls cite the same ten sources. All three v12 answers could retain those ten, add an unrelated source as support, and change the forecast within the same range. Neither flag would fire. Freeze what counts as material harm and what evidence from the fresh controls makes a difference repeatable or leaves it unresolved. The saved answer can help locate changes. The fresh controls are the comparison. [Part C rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:64)\n\n2. **State the pass line as a tolerance for this probe.** Two of 48 is defensible as a proposed maximum for these selected draws. The 17 original refusals were selected because they failed, and three draws of one request can repeat the same mistake. Neither supports the claimed 4% historical rate. Count each answer with a confirmed wrong attribution once, and report how many of the 16 requests were affected and whether the error repeated. Require all 48 Part B answers and all 16 complete Part C comparisons for a pass. A budget stop, missing control, or unresolved material citation loss makes the result inconclusive. Keep zero refusals among the required v12 answers and zero confirmed material harm in Part C. [Outcome rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:72)\n\n3. **Keep the core sends and give the optional size check last priority.** I verified 16 distinct Part B requests and 16 distinct Part C matches. `8941` is `8938` with the retry note. The seven linked requests are valid format-only comparisons when both sends keep the same v8 text and change only the answer format. The matching code chooses the nearest call on either side, despite its stated earlier-call tie rule. That changes two selections, so document which rule you intend. A1 exercises the empty dependency list. For a separate empty-list check, `old-3:69` also exercises an empty theme list at an estimated cost under $0.001. Keep sealed `6918` for spare budget. A success shows that this large request fits. A rejection establishes an enum limit only if the provider’s error says so. [Matching code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_plan.py:73) · [Send plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:17)\n\n   The saved-token estimate is **$0.427 for 146 sends**. The ledger reserves per attempt, including retries, and reserves **$0.0824** for `6918` alone. Sending the two formats together does not guarantee a complete comparison. Freeze the send order and what happens to partial comparisons. If the plan promises to start only comparisons that can finish under the cap, prove that schedule with the actual reservations before committing to it. [Reservation code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:227) · [Retry code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:262)\n\n4. **Run one full $0 rehearsal before sending.** Stub the provider beneath the real budget transport. Verify all scheduled sends reach that stub with the expected bytes, strict format and source lists. `model.call` normally reuses identical requests, so count actual stub calls to prove all three draws are fresh. Run `check_answer` against the state shown at the time of each request. I verified that using the archive’s final state falsely rejects two saved linked controls, `8834` and `8851`. Exercise a valid answer, an invalid answer, an HTTP 400, a retry, and a cap stop mid-comparison. Confirm that an incomplete run cannot produce a pass. [Model cache](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:253) · [Judgement checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:259)\n\nFreeze the revised rules and show that the $0 rehearsal catches the dropped 85.4% estimate and refuses to pass an incomplete comparison. This was a read-only review. No files changed and no paid calls were made."}}
